{
  "full_prompt_html": "<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Act as an experienced people manager, an HR business partner and an executive coach.</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">I need to have a performance conversation with a member of my team. Help me prepare. [Paste the facts with names removed: the expected standard, what happened, dates, examples and any earlier conversations.] [Paste the relevant role expectations or policy, if you have them.]</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Prepare me in four parts:</span></p>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>1. Separate Facts from Judgments</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nList the observable facts: what happened, when, and the effect on the team, clients or results.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nIdentify each statement in my notes that is an opinion or an assumption, and rewrite it as a fact or remove it.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nState the gap between the expected standard and the actual performance in one sentence.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>2. Plan the Conversation</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nWrite an opening of no more than three sentences that states the purpose directly.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nList three open questions that let the employee explain their view.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nSuggest what support, resources or changes I can offer.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>3. Anticipate Responses</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nPredict the four most likely reactions, such as disagreement, surprise, emotion or blaming others.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nFor each one, give a calm, specific response that keeps the conversation on the facts.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nFlag anything that suggests a wellbeing, accommodation or policy issue that needs HR involvement before the meeting.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 6pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(34, 31, 31);\"><b>4. Agree the Next Steps</b></span></p>\n<ul data-editing-info=\"{&quot;applyListStyleFromLevel&quot;:true}\" style=\"margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; list-style-type: disc;\">\n<li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nDraft two or three measurable expectations with dates.</div>\n</li><li style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52); margin: 0in 0in 6pt;\">\n<div class=\"elementToProof\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"margin-top: 0in; margin-bottom: 6pt;\">\nDraft a short follow-up email that records what we agreed, in neutral language.</div>\n</li></ul>\n<p class=\"elementToProof\" style=\"margin: 0in 0in 9pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">\n<span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt; color: rgb(58, 54, 52);\">Deliver a one-page conversation plan with the opening, the questions, the likely responses and the next steps, followed by the follow-up email. Use plain, respectful language. Do not give legal advice; tell me where I should check with HR.</span></p>",
  "n": 4,
  "subject_area": "HR and people ops",
  "summary": "Prepare for a performance conversation by separating facts from judgments, planning the opening, anticipating reactions, and agreeing measurable next steps.",
  "title": "Prepare for a difficult conversation about an employee’s performance"
}
